# English-only code, comments, and user-facing strings

Every line of source code, comment, log message, dialog title, button label,
warning text, error string, or other user-facing string that you add to this
project must be in **English only**. This applies to:

- `self.log(...)` and `self.outlog(...)` strings.
- `QMessageBox` / `QInputDialog` text and titles.
- Comments inside `.py`, `.js`, `.ini`, `.md` files.
- Docstrings and inline help text.
- Exception messages constructed for the UI.

## Why

- The project already ships Chinese and English `.qm` translation files; any
  hard-coded Chinese in source bypasses the translation system and shows up
  in the UI for English users.
- Mixed-language log files make it hard to grep / share / paste to issues.
- English keeps the code accessible to outside contributors and AI tooling.

## Concrete examples

```python
# ❌ BAD
self.log("附加异常,application is None err:%s" % err)
QMessageBox().warning(self, "提示", "请先选择已连接的手机")

# ✅ GOOD
self.log("attach failed: application is None err=%s" % err)
QMessageBox().warning(self, "Hint", "Please select a connected device first")
```

```python
# ❌ BAD
def checkFridaDeviceAlignment(self, packageName):
    # 检查端口转发是否指向了旧的 frida-server
    ...

# ✅ GOOD
def checkFridaDeviceAlignment(self, packageName):
    # Verify that the port-forward is not pointing to a stale frida-server.
    ...
```

```js
// ❌ BAD
console.log("抓包完成，共 " + count + " 条");

// ✅ GOOD
console.log("capture complete, " + count + " entries");
```

## What stays in Chinese

- Existing user-facing strings in `_translate("...")` lookup calls (those go
  through the translation files).
- Comments inside `forms/` .qm source files (translation tables, not code).
- Any legacy string that is already wrapped in `self._translate(...)` /
  `self.trText(...)` — these are translated automatically and must NOT be
  rewritten as English.

If you need to display a message that should be localized, wrap it in
`self._translate("module","English source")` so the English source becomes the
fallback and Chinese translators can provide a `.qm` entry. Do NOT inline
Chinese in source code.

## Pre-commit mental check

Before finishing a code change, scan your added lines for any CJK characters
(`一-鿿` or `぀-ゟ゠-ヿ` ranges). If any are present outside `.qm` files,
replace them with English.